Package: open-couch-engine
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 systemd,
 pulseaudio-utils,
# gamescope lives in contrib on Debian and universe on Ubuntu, so a hard
# dependency would make this package uninstallable on a stock Debian. It is a
# Recommends instead: apt still pulls it in wherever it is available, and
# "open-couch-engine doctor" reports a missing one better than an unmet
# dependency would. steam is non-free and heavy; a Suggests is enough.
Recommends:
 gamescope,
Suggests:
 steam,
 open-couch,
Description: console mode for your Linux desktop - the engine
 Open Couch hands the whole machine to Steam's gamescope session on the
 television and gives it back cleanly when you leave.
 .
 This package is the engine: a static binary with no runtime dependencies that
 hosts your desktop and the gamescope session in one login session, switches
 between them, and puts the sound and the display back on the way home. It does
 everything from the command line and does not need the graphical application.
 .
 A gamescope-session package from the distribution is required at runtime; the
 engine detects a missing one and reports it with "open-couch-engine doctor"
 rather than failing to install.

